From: MediaTek vendor feed <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_ppe: add binding bypass by ct mark 0x99

Port of MediaTek vendor patch 999-ppe-36 (mtk-openwrt-feeds,
25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12). Filed locally as
999-ppe-93, not 999-ppe-36: this fork already has an unrelated,
self-invented local patch at that number
(999-ppe-36-mtk-eth-enable-pppq-qos-by-default-for-netsysv1.patch,
predating this port). Adapted for this
tree's mtk_ppe.h: the vendor's hunk assumes mtk_ppe.h includes
"mtk_eth_soc.h" and inserts MTK_PPE_EXCEPTION_TAG right after that
include; this tree's mtk_ppe.h has a different header layout (no
mtk_eth_soc.h include at that point), so the define is inserted before
MTK_PPE_ENTRIES_SHIFT instead - same net effect, no functional change.
The mtk_ppe_offload.c hunk (mtk_flow_offload_replace()) is unmodified;
f->flow->ct is already an established access pattern in this exact
file (see mtk_flow_set_output_device()).

Without this patch, there is no way to prevent specific connections
from being hardware-offloaded by the PPE.

Users can mark 0x99 to conntrack entry to bypass PPE binding using
`nft ... ct mark set 0x99`. No chip-version gate.

Directly relevant to the open question in
docs/e8450-download-shaping-handoff.md (does a WiFi client's
PPE-hardware-offloaded download bypass CAKE shaping): marking a known
flow's conntrack entry with 0x99 keeps it off PPE hardware offload
permanently, giving a declarative test/mitigation instead of relying
solely on the reactive occupancy-driven eviction in 999-qos-06. See
docs/e8450-mtk-feeds-audit-2026-09.md S4.

Signed-off-by: MediaTek vendor feed <noreply@example.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.h
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/bitfield.h>
 #include <linux/rhashtable.h>
 
+#define MTK_PPE_EXCEPTION_TAG		0x99
 #define MTK_PPE_ENTRIES_SHIFT		4
 #define MTK_PPE_ENTRIES			(1024 << MTK_PPE_ENTRIES_SHIFT)
 #define MTK_PPE_HASH_MASK		(MTK_PPE_ENTRIES - 1)
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
@@ -423,4 +423,7 @@ mtk_flow_offload_replace(struct mtk_eth
 	if (rhashtable_lookup(&eth->flow_table, &f->cookie, mtk_flow_ht_params))
 		return -EEXIST;
 
+	if (f->flow && f->flow->ct && f->flow->ct->mark == MTK_PPE_EXCEPTION_TAG)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
 	if (flow_rule_match_key(rule, FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_META)) {
